**VERIFY PASS — phase-082**, 0 failures (1 WARN, explained below).

What this run found and did:

**Root cause of the retry's failure.** `verify.sh` diffs against `HEAD`. The previous attempt's work had been committed into the resume checkpoint `cd7aed7`, so the tree was clean and the test scanner read `0 / 0 / 0` — the same fact as its `no changed files detected against HEAD` failure, not a broken scanner. FINDINGS.md §4 was wrong and is now corrected with the measurements.

**Three `tests/doc_blocks_test.rs` tests were already failing on arrival.** 49 of the 101 `doc:line` keys in the bucket files named no block (phase-089 moved 17 lines in `SPEC.md` / 21 in `docs/GRAMMAR.md` without re-pointing them). Rebuilt by measurement: all 105 blocks extracted and run under both `rb run` and `rb compile`. 62 RUNS / 40 FRAGMENT / 3 KNOWN-FAIL.

**`quote_opens_a_string` was wrong in the permissive direction.** It reported a `'` inside a `//` comment — and `SPEC.md:143` writes `// LexerError: Unknown escape '\q' in text` — while relying on a one-character look-behind. Rewritten as a real code/text/comment scan.

**12 new `#[test]`** (11 `edge_*`), 6 failure-asserting: the all-buckets quote scan, the buckets-cover-the-documents invariant, the directory half of README's tree (was never checked), each correction located by content and required to be `RUNS`, and four `#[should_panic]` refusals on the bucket reader. Four mutations were run and reverted to confirm the teeth — the missing-directory mutation fails the new test and only the new test.

Gates: `fmt` clean, `clippy -D warnings` clean, `cargo test` **1808 passed, 0 failed**, `verify.sh` PASS.

The one WARN is `report honesty` reading `1555` — `verify.sh` reads `REPORT.md` one level above the checkout, which the phase contract forbids writing. The report I wrote is at `phases/phase-082/REPORT.md` and claims 1808. Recorded in FINDINGS.md § 7.

